      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The eight optically active stereoisomers and the corresponding four racemic forms of 5,9-dimethyl-2'-hydroxy-2-tetrahydrofurfuryl-6,7-benzomorphan (1) have been prepared. Depending on their configurations these compounds are potent analgesics or inactive substances in mice. The analgesics attain potencies up to about a hundred times that of morphine but they do not show morphine-like side effects in mice nor do they suppress abstinence in withdrawn morphine dependent monkeys. Their therapeutic ratios are favorable and, in the case of la-1 and la-2, exceptionally good. Configuration-activity relationships are discussed. R configuration of the N-tetrahydrofurfuryl group is a major prerequisite for high analgesic potency."},
